## Context

Model behaviour diverges where skill text leaves execution shape
unspecified. Controlled observation, raid of 2026-06-04: raid Phases
2/3 say "launch an agent (background)" — the orchestrator (Opus 4.8)
fanned out planners and executes without prompting; Phase 6 says only
"invoke /verify <pr> on each merge request" — the same orchestrator
serialized four verifies. An earlier model (4.7) parallelized the same
phase by disposition. IDH is model-agnostic: the skill text, not the
model's temperament, must be the contract.

Author directive (2026-06-04): adjust skill language to encourage the
intended parallelism for every model.

## Relevant files

- `rules/workflow.md` § Writing Skills and Hooks — new general principle
- `skills/raid/SKILL.md` Phase 6 — the concrete underdetermined step
- tickets/0193 — sub-agent cwd pinning; gates the default flip

## Actions

1. rules/workflow.md, § Writing Skills: add the principle — "State
   concurrency explicitly. Every multi-item skill step declares whether
   items run parallel-background or sequential-blocking, and why. Model
   defaults differ across versions; the skill text is the contract."
   (Lands independently, immediately.)
2. skills/raid/SKILL.md Phase 6: "Launch per-ticket /verify runs in
   parallel (background agents, one per merge request) when the PR
   branches touch disjoint files; verify file-sharing PRs sequentially.
   Respect the max-concurrent-agents cap. Phase 7 merges stay strictly
   sequential." Include, until 0193 lands, the caveat that each parallel
   verify runner is instructed not to repair foreign branch state it
   encounters.
3. Sweep other multi-item skill steps (healthcheck sweeps, review-pr
   fan-out, dream) for the same underdetermination; annotate each with
   its intended mode.

## Test

Grep-able: `grep -n "parallel" skills/raid/SKILL.md` includes Phase 6;
`grep -n "concurrency" rules/workflow.md` hits the new principle.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Writing-Skills principle present in rules/workflow.md
- [x] Raid Phase 6 declares parallel fan-out + sequential-merge contract
- [x] One sweep pass over existing skills' multi-item steps documented in this ticket's log
